    "text": "Latest AIN (Aviation International Magazine- september2026) shows Embraer (Brazilian) Phenom 300EV aircraft, is the first business jet to receive certification for Garmin Avionics Co. - \"Emergency Autoland\" under the program's certification by ANAC (Brazil), FAA (US), and EASA (Europe).\n\nWhat \"Emergency Autoland\" does:\n\nIf the pilot becomes incapacitated, a passenger can activate Emergency Autoland, or the system can activate automatically depending on the aircraft/system configuration.\n\nIt can:\nPilot incapacitated\n       ↓\nEmergency Autoland\n       ↓\nSelects suitable airport\n       ↓\nCalculates flight path\n       ↓\nCommunicates with ATC (air traffic control)\n       ↓\nDescends\n       ↓\nApproach\n       ↓\nLANDS\n       ↓\nStops aircraft\n\nIt is designed to take the aircraft through the entire emergency sequence to landing.\n\nANAC + FAA + EASA certification is significant because the system has been evaluated by the Brazilian, US and European aviation certification authorities—not merely approved by Garmin or Embraer themselves.\n\nThis is a boost for executive business jets.",
