    "handle": "Bellotsoho",
    "name": "SHUNI",
    "text": "Sokoto State Becomes the 6th State in Nigeria to Own an Airline as Caliphate Air Takes Delivery of an ERJ 190 ✈️🇳🇬\n\nSokoto State is taking another significant step into Nigeria’s aviation industry as its state-backed airline, Caliphate Air, takes delivery of a new Embraer E190 aircraft in Abuja.\n\nThe arrival of the aircraft marks another milestone in the development of Caliphate Air, which is being positioned as a major link between Sokoto, the wider Northwest and other parts of Nigeria\n\nThe airline is building its operations around Abuja as its hub, with plans to connect cities including Sokoto, Kano, Gusau, Birnin Kebbi, Maiduguri, Yola, Lagos and Port Harcourt. Its initial network is designed to improve connectivity between major commercial, administrative and cultural centres across the country.\n\nFor Sokoto, the significance goes beyond owning an airline. Better air connectivity can make it easier for investors, business travellers, tourists, government officials and development partners to access the state, while also supporting the movement of people and economic activities across the Northwest.\nThe E190, which offers significantly greater capacity than the airline's ERJ-145 aircraft, also gives Caliphate Air room to serve routes with stronger passenger demand as the network grows. The airline says the aircraft seats between 96 and 114 passengers depending on configuration.\n\nWith its fleet taking shape and Abuja established as its operational hub, Caliphate Air is positioning itself for a new chapter in Nigerian domestic aviation.\n\nThank Gov Ahmad Aliyu Sokoto  PhD, fcna.\n\n#TourNigeria #worldscapenigeria  #Aviationnews #InfrastructureDevelopment #CaliphateAir #SokotoState #ERJ190 #NigerianAviation #Aviation #Nigeria #Sokoto #Abuja #ExploreNigeria",
