    "text": "Airlink’s Embraer E195 aircraft conducted a planned flypast over Cape Town’s DHL Stadium on August 29, 2026, during the Springboks vs All Blacks rugby match. Videos circulating online show the aircraft appearing to pass at a very low altitude over the packed stadium, raising questions among aviation observers about the actual flight path and clearance used. While the flypast was clearly a coordinated operation, claims that the first aircraft cleared the roof by only a few metres or that the second aircraft was struck by pyrotechnics have not been independently confirmed by Airlink or an aviation authority. The operation highlights the importance of precise flight-path planning, minimum-clearance requirements and airspace coordination for stadium flypasts.\n\n#airlink #embraer #e195 #aviationnews #aveonews",
