    "handle": "tengizlab",
    "name": "Tengiz",
    "text": "The Chinese COMAC C919 undergoing a full-scale ultimate-load test.\n\nAircraft wings are designed to flex under load. The important question is how far they can flex while still carrying the loads they are designed for.\n\nEngineers loaded a full-scale C919 test aircraft to a 2.5g maneuver condition, then increased the load to 150% of limit load  the ultimate-load level. The wingtip deflected nearly 3 meters, while engineers measured strain and deformation throughout the test.\n\nThe point wasn't simply to see whether the wing would break. Engineers were checking whether the actual structure behaved as predicted by their structural analysis and whether it could withstand the required ultimate load.\n\nThe C919 test structure met the required strength and deformation criteria at the 150% load level.\n\nThat's what a full-scale structural test provides: the analysis predicts how the structure should behave, and the test shows whether the measured behavior agrees with those predictions.",
