    "text": "25 December 2025: Azerbaijan Airlines Flight 8243 took off from Baku, bound for Grozny but never made it.\n\nThe aircraft, an Embraer E190, was carrying 67 people onboard. As it approached Grozny, it lost navigation systems (GPS interference) and faced poor weather conditions.\n\nDuring the approach, a shrapnel impact hit the aircraft and the crew attempted to divert and perform an emergency landing in Aktau.\n\nCritical aircraft systems including the hydraulics gave up, leading to loss of control before the crash.  \n\nInvestigations later confirmed something serious:..\nThe aircraft was accidentally hit by a Russian air-defense system during active military operations and Russia eventually acknowledged it was an “unintentional strike” and agreed to compensation in 2026.\n\nThis is one of the rare modern cases of a civilian airliner being unintentionally shot down. Raising major concerns about civil aviation safety in conflict zones.",
