    "text": "Impressive and so useful for humanity: \n\nChina’s “Five Senses Health Aircraft Hospital\" is a major breakthrough in mobile healthcare.\n\nThe project is a collaborative effort between COMAC (the Commercial Aircraft Corporation of China) and the Eye & ENT Hospital of Fudan University in Shanghai.\nEngineers modified a homegrown COMAC C909 commercial jetliner.\n\nThe plane utilizes an innovative, bolt-free modular installation system. This allows technicians to completely transform the passenger cabin into a fully functional medical center in just eight hours. \n\nThe plane is equipped with a Class I sterile operating cabin. This represents the highest tier of medical cleanliness standards, effectively matching a top-tier stationary hospital cleanroom. \n\nDelicate ophthalmic and micro-ENT surgeries require absolute physical stability. The aircraft operates as a mobile clinic that flies to remote regions, lands at local airports, and hosts procedures on the ground. \n\nThe aircraft features advanced 5G remote diagnosis and treatment systems. This allows top specialists stationed back in Shanghai to monitor procedures and guide local teams in real time. \n\nThe aircraft made its inaugural medical mission to Shihezi, Xinjiang, where nearly 50 patients received specialized examinations and treatment directly onboard. \n\nIn early 2026, the project officially received its Medical Institution Practice Licensefrom Shanghai authorities, transitioning from a prototype to an authorized flying hospital. \n\nUnder China's \"Health Silk Road in the Sky\" initiative, the plane has expanded its reach beyond China. It has completed charitable missions in Laos and recently touched down in Almaty, Kazakhstan, having served over 1,700 total patients.",
