    "text": "Delivery of the next-generation Air Force One has slipped again, with the first aircraft now not expected until mid-2028. The revised timeline raises the possibility that Donald Trump may never fly on the new jet during his presidency.\n\nThe program, led by Boeing under a $3.9 billion contract with the United States Air Force, was originally meant to deliver the first aircraft by December 2024. That date has already slid to 2027 and is now being discussed as mid-2028, following technical and structural challenges during modification.\n\nThe aircraft, designated VC-25B and based on the Boeing 747-8, is intended to replace the current VC-25A fleet that has served since the early 1990s. Until delivery, the existing Air Force One aircraft will continue operating well beyond their planned service life.",
