    "text": "A United Airlines Boeing 737-900 operating Flight UA1936 declared a general emergency during its approach to Houston on Sunday afternoon.\n\nThe aircraft, registered N35407, departed Ontario International Airport bound for George Bush Intercontinental Airport. While descending over Texas at around 20,000 feet, the crew squawked 7700, signaling a general emergency to air traffic control.\n\nDespite the alert, the pilots continued a controlled approach and landed safely on Runway 8R at Houston at 11:02 CST, roughly two hours and 34 minutes after departure. No injuries were reported, and United has not disclosed the reason for the emergency.\n\nSuch declarations are precautionary and allow crews priority handling and emergency services on standby, even when the situation ultimately resolves without incident.",
