    "name": "Flightdrama",
    "text": "Regional aircraft lessor TrueNoord has placed its first-ever direct order with a manufacturer, agreeing to purchase 20 new Embraer E195-E2 aircraft. The deal, announced this week, also includes purchase rights for 20 more E195-E2s and up to 10 E175s. At list prices, the firm order is valued at $1.8 billion.\n\nTrueNoord CEO Anne-Bart Tieleman called the move a “milestone” for the Amsterdam-based lessor, highlighting the aircraft’s efficiency and environmental benefits. “It marks an important stepping stone in our continued growth as a global leasing platform,” he said.\n\nEmbraer’s commercial chief Arjan Meijer said the order reflects strong confidence in the E2 family, which has been marketed as the most fuel-efficient single-aisle jets in their class. “This sends a strong signal to the market,” he added, noting demand for right-sized, sustainable aircraft is growing.\n\nThe new jets will be offered to airlines worldwide as TrueNoord expands its portfolio beyond traditional lease acquisitions.",
